00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:30,020
 And the cache key is the thing that determines what a unique page is as far as caching goes.

39
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:35,320
 And you can see some of the things that are in CloudFlare's cache key by default are things

40
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:40,940
 like the X method override header, X HTTP method override header, the sort of things that will

41
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:45,020
 break the backend probably if they're included, right?

42
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,140
